  "answer": "- **Stop outdoor observations when the wind interlock opens.** Preserve reservation identifiers during the suspension.\n- **Restart only after both** the interlock closes and the duty operator records restart approval. A favourable forecast is not an interlock signal and cannot authorize a restart.\n- **An indoor instrument may continue** during the wind suspension if it is explicitly classified as indoor and its own safety interlocks remain closed. A roof shown as closed on the calendar does not establish that classification.\n\nSource: [Weather decisions — Suspension, Indoor instrument, and Forecast display](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vanilla1999/DocAtlas/e62fa9e357bd22731cddabe930532a4a2faecc18/eval/blind_project_context/step14-host-language-live/frozen-corpus/weather.md).",
